// The editor locus, second half: which tool *holds* a gated file type.
// `editor-extensions.json` installs the extension; this decides that the
// extension is the one that runs. They are separate artefacts because they are
// separate claims — an extension was installed the whole time another one held
// the file type, and LNT-001 called that a pass (ADR 0029 point 4).
//
// **Workspace scope, and only workspace scope.** Write this to
// `.vscode/settings.json` in the repository, never into `devcontainer.json`.
// The containers.dev merge table gives one instruction for `customizations` —
// "Merging is left to the tools" — where every other property states a rule, so
// a binding written there lands in the same machine-scoped file a devcontainer
// feature's does and competes on undefined terms. A tracked workspace file wins
// by documented rule instead (ADR 0029 point 1). The checker fails a repository
// that sets this binding in both places, agreement included: agreeing today is
// luck, not a rule.
//
// **A missing binding is a violation, not a default.** The state this catches
// is the one where nothing tracked said anything and a devcontainer feature
// decided — `ghcr.io/devcontainers/features/python:1` published
//   "[python]": { "editor.defaultFormatter": "ms-python.autopep8" }
// in a repository whose register pinned ruff. DEV-001's digest pin governs what
// a feature installs and says nothing about what it configures, so nothing saw
// it. Say the binding rather than correct one.
//
// Every value is the register's: the language and the setting are
// `stacks.{{STACK}}.gates.lint.editor_binding`, and the extension is that
// gate's `editor_extension`. A gate whose register entry declares no
// `editor_binding` binds no file type, and this artefact is not written for it
// — eslint is a linter and not TypeScript's formatter.
//
// LNT-001 is the only one of this gate's three controls declaring an `editor`
// locus, so the stamp names it alone.
//
// --- .vscode/settings.json — merged into what is already there ---
{
  // ee-control: LNT-001  ee-skill: gate-quality@{{SKILL_VERSION}}  register: v{{REGISTER_VERSION}}  register-contract: {{REGISTER_CONTRACT}}
  "[{{EDITOR_LANGUAGE}}]": {
    "{{EDITOR_BINDING_SETTING}}": "{{EDITOR_EXTENSION}}"
  }
}
